{
  "name": "FluxFilm · 03 Daily encrypted backup → Google Drive",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔐 FluxFilm daily backup — SETUP\n**Every day 02:30 India time**: downloads an **encrypted** backup of the whole shop database (`fluxfilm-backup-YYYY-MM-DD.ffbak`), uploads it to the Google Drive folder **FluxFilm Backups**, and moves backups **older than 30 days** to the Drive bin. If anything fails you get an email.\n\n1. In admin → 🔗 Integrations set a **backup passphrase** (write it down! without it a backup cannot be opened).\n2. Credentials: `FluxFilm n8n key` (Header Auth), `Google Drive FluxFilm` (Google Drive OAuth2), `SMTP FluxFilm (Gmail app password)`.\n3. In Google Drive make a folder **FluxFilm Backups**. Open it, copy the id from the address (after `/folders/`) and paste it into **Upload to Drive** and **List old backups** (replace `REPLACE_WITH_FOLDER_ID`).\n4. Put your email in **Email owner: backup failed**.\n5. **Execute workflow** once, check the file is in Drive, then **Active** on.\n\nOpen a backup on your computer: `node scripts/restore-backup.js fluxfilm-backup-2026-09-17.ffbak out` (asks for the passphrase).\nBig database later? Use GET /n8n/api/backup/tables + /n8n/api/backup?table=<name> in a loop (README).",
        "height": 500,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "2465dbbe-cc45-4ab8-ac8c-1f31a2b32df0",
      "name": "Setup: daily backup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -480,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "30 2 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "cf9d3693-0df5-4774-ae57-f217c5f1d155",
      "name": "Every day 02:30 IST",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://shop.fluxfilm.in/n8n/api/backup",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 170000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "file",
              "outputPropertyName": "data"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "860c6fc2-1524-4549-a2e4-03e9773cc0d1",
      "name": "Download encrypted backup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "FluxFilm n8n key"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// The shop sends the name in Content-Disposition; build the same name if n8n lost it.\nconst d = new Date(Date.now() + 5.5 * 3600e3).toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst bin = $input.item.binary && $input.item.binary.data;\nif (!bin) throw new Error('No backup file came back');\nconst size = Number(bin.fileSize ? String(bin.fileSize).replace(/[^0-9.]/g, '') : 0);\nbin.fileName = 'fluxfilm-backup-' + d + '.ffbak';\nbin.mimeType = 'application/octet-stream';\nreturn { json: { fileName: bin.fileName, size: bin.fileSize || '' }, binary: { data: bin } };"
      },
      "id": "1b15ad52-58dd-4493-a594-72ed96f4aacd",
      "name": "Name the file",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "name": "={{ $json.fileName }}",
        "driveId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "My Drive"
        },
        "folderId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "REPLACE_WITH_FOLDER_ID"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "3f7758e7-67e2-42db-a110-966cdfe53f7a",
      "name": "Upload to Drive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDrive",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        720,
        -100
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googleDriveOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "Google Drive FluxFilm"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "fileFolder",
        "searchMethod": "query",
        "queryString": "'REPLACE_WITH_FOLDER_ID' in parents and name contains 'fluxfilm-backup-' and trashed = false",
        "returnAll": true,
        "filter": {},
        "options": {
          "fields": [
            "id",
            "name",
            "createdTime"
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "19bbdd0f-cfaf-4c35-a41d-5434307ae429",
      "name": "List old backups",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDrive",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        960,
        -160
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googleDriveOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "Google Drive FluxFilm"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const cutoff = Date.now() - 30 * 86400e3;\nconst old = $input.all().filter((i) => i.json.id && i.json.createdTime && Date.parse(i.json.createdTime) < cutoff);\n// Never delete the newest backups even if the clock is wrong: keep at least 7 files.\nconst all = $input.all().filter((i) => i.json.id).sort((a, b) => String(b.json.createdTime).localeCompare(String(a.json.createdTime)));\nconst keep = new Set(all.slice(0, 7).map((i) => i.json.id));\nreturn old.filter((i) => !keep.has(i.json.id)).map((i) => ({ json: { id: i.json.id, name: i.json.name } }));"
      },
      "id": "17ab367a-062c-4293-a2c2-fc9c005c484f",
      "name": "Older than 30 days",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1200,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "deleteFile",
        "fileId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $json.id }}"
        },
        "options": {
          "deletePermanently": false
        }
      },
      "id": "c49dcc57-3fff-4652-abda-7e82d526f97f",
      "name": "Move old backup to bin",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDrive",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        1440,
        -160
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googleDriveOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "Google Drive FluxFilm"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const err = $input.first().json.error || $input.first().json;\nconst msg = typeof err === 'string' ? err : (err.message || JSON.stringify(err).slice(0, 400));\nreturn [{ json: { subject: '❌ FluxFilm backup FAILED ' + new Date(Date.now() + 5.5 * 3600e3).toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace('T', ' '), text: 'The daily backup did not finish.\\n\\n' + msg + '\\n\\nCheck: backup passphrase set in admin → 🔗 Integrations, the n8n key, Google Drive login, and n8n Executions.' } }];"
      },
      "id": "e669e14e-cbd8-4dea-a7f3-cd4b7f926a05",
      "name": "Failure message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        720,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "fromEmail": "FluxFilm <REPLACE_WITH_SENDER@gmail.com>",
        "toEmail": "REPLACE_WITH_OWNER_EMAIL@example.com",
        "subject": "={{ $json.subject }}",
        "emailFormat": "html",
        "html": "={{ '<pre style=\"font-family:system-ui;white-space:pre-wrap\">' + $json.text.replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</pre>' }}",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "dc6541fa-142a-4cd2-a774-0c0efd0c3c9f",
      "name": "Email owner: backup failed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailSend",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        960,
        140
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "smtp": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "SMTP FluxFilm (Gmail app password)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID",
        "text": "={{ $json.subject + '\\n' + $json.text }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "0dcce5ed-c0da-4763-a5b5-6564dc9868e3",
      "name": "Telegram owner: backup failed (disabled)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        960,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "Telegram FluxFilm bot"
        }
      },
      "disabled": true
    }
  ],
